{"data": {"id": "5e5797826c50533639f8f8782fdc798141e555766e890344010cf3f278a9d479", "lineage": "5e5797826c50533639f8f8782fdc798141e555766e890344010cf3f278a9d479", "origin": "sample:4", "parent": null, "source": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic final class Solution {\n    public static Object solve(Map<String, Object> data) {\n        Object gridObj = data.get(\"grid\");\n        if (gridObj == null || gridObj instanceof List<?> && ((List<?>) gridObj).isEmpty()) {\n            return 0;\n        }\n        List<List<?>> grid = (List<List<?>>) gridObj;\n        int rows = grid.size();\n        if (rows == 0) {\n            return 0;\n        }\n        int cols = grid.get(0).size();\n        \n        Number start = (Number) grid.get(0).get(0);\n        if (start.intValue() == 1) {\n            return 0;\n        }\n        \n        int[][] dp = new int[rows][cols];\n        dp[0][0] = 1;\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < rows; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < cols; j++) {\n                if (i == 0 && j == 0) {\n                    continue;\n                }\n                Number cell = (Number) grid.get(i).get(j);\n                if (cell.intValue() == 1) {\n                    dp[i][j] = 0;\n                } else {\n                    int top = (i > 0) ? dp[i-1][j] : 0;\n                    int left = (j > 0) ? dp[i][j-1] : 0;\n                    dp[i][j] = top + left;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return dp[rows-1][cols-1];\n    }\n}"}, "kind": "candidate", "prev": "638d8426bd9f5ec9ca106b817b49492fc757f4abe593b00be062c363997132ef", "seq": 30}
